      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A single coronary artery is a very rare type of coronary artery anomaly that may present in various forms. A patient is presented in whom the right coronary artery coursed as the terminal branch of the left circumflex artery. This is the second case of this anomaly in the literature."},
